WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.327 --> 00:00:04.260
[INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC] JOSEPH&nbsp;
BETANCOURT: How does your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:08.140
organization address racial equity&nbsp;
and access to health care delivery?

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:12.000
ASWITA TAN-MCGRORY: For decades, researchers&nbsp;
have studied the differences in quality of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.160
care between people of color and their white&nbsp;
counterparts. They lead to poorer health&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:22.560
outcomes and exemplify low-value health care.&nbsp;
Together with the Disparity . Solution Center&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:28.680
at Massachusetts General Hospital, this course&nbsp;
uses case studies and insights from leaders&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:33.046
so you can create strategic approaches&nbsp;
that you can apply to your organization.

00:00:33.046 --> 00:00:36.780
ALVIN POWELL: The history is the&nbsp;
reason for the disparities. There's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:41.801
no other reason for the disparities&nbsp;
other than our American history.

00:00:41.801 --> 00:00:49.380
MITCHELL KELLAWAY: There can be this sense that&nbsp;
we're doing everything right, so all of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:54.827
disparity is somewhere out there. But we need to&nbsp;
be really honest with ourselves when it's at home.

00:00:54.827 --> 00:01:00.420
ALTAF SAADI: And a really important part&nbsp;
of implementing any policy or action at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:02.940
your organization or health care facility&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:06.466
is understanding that it's a&nbsp;
process. It doesn't happen overnight.

00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:10.740
ALVIN POWELL: It's the systemic and&nbsp;
structural racism that has existed for all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:15.100
of these years that has created these significant&nbsp;
disparities that we continue to deal with today.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:17.760
ASWITA TAN-MCGRORY: To really&nbsp;
drive organizational change,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:23.561
we have to include people from the top of&nbsp;
our organization all the way to the bottom.

00:01:23.561 --> 00:01:27.420
JOSEPH BETANCOURT: Learn how to lead your&nbsp;
health care organization in tackling these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:33.480
systemic problems and improving patient equity&nbsp;
with reducing racial disparities in health care.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:33.927
[Music]

